# Ticket test documentation

When you **complete**, **hand off**, or **close** work tied to a GitHub issue (or PR that fixes an issue), add a **Test plan** section so the next person can reproduce verification without re-deriving steps from the diff.

## Where to document

| Location | When |
|----------|------|
| **GitHub issue comment** | Default — post before close or with final PR link |
| **PR description** | Include the same checklist under `## Test plan` |
| **ADR / design doc** | Only for locked acceptance criteria — link issue; do not duplicate full play steps |

Do not mark an exploration/combat issue done without at least one **automated** or **manual** verification path recorded.

## Test plan template

```markdown
## Test plan (verified YYYY-MM-DD)

### Automated
- [ ] Unity Test Runner → Edit Mode → `<Category>` → `<TestClass>` — all green (categories: game repo [Assets/Tests/README.md](../../../griddungeon-game/Assets/Tests/README.md))
- [ ] (optional) Play Mode / CI — note job or N/A

### Manual (Play Mode)
- **Scene:** `DevBootstrap.unity` (local only — **GridDungeon → Scenes → Create Dev Bootstrap** after clone)
- **Setup:** `<F2 Exploration, InputRouter wired, …>`
- **Steps:**
  1. …
  2. …
- **Expected:** …

### Regressions checked
- [ ] …

### Spec / ADRs
- [ADR 001](link), [ADR 018](link), …
```

## Grid Dungeon defaults (exploration)

Unless the ticket changes timings, assume **Normal** preset (design-docs [ADR 018](../../griddungeon-design-docs/decisions/018-exploration-animation-speed.md)): step **0.28s**, turn **0.26s**, hold-to-repeat per [ADR 001](../../griddungeon-design-docs/decisions/001-grid-movement.md).

**Dev bootstrap:** `GridDungeon → Scenes → Create Dev Bootstrap` if scene refs are stale; **F1** Hub / **F2** Exploration / **F3** Combat.

## Agent / PR workflow

1. Run applicable **Edit Mode** tests when the change touches `GridDungeon.Core` or testable rules.
2. After implementation, **post the filled template** to the issue via `gh issue comment` (or PR body).
3. If the user verified in-editor, incorporate their notes; do not invent results you did not run.
